{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A sword.</b> Its sense is a decree." "<b>It is fattened.</b> A compound word, from a binyan whose verbal noun is not called and from the nif'al binyan, according to the opinion of many. This is not correct. Rather, it is a foreign word, and its sense is from the root of והיה דשן ושמן (Isaiah 30:23)." "<b>Rams.</b> Like חלב כרים (Deuteronomy 32:14), a metaphorical expression for the great, like אילי מואב (Exodus 15:15)." "<b>In Bozrah.</b> Some say it is Constantinople. This is impossible, for it was founded less than a thousand years ago. Rather, it is a city in the land of Edom."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {3 "The timing argument only makes sense from a 12th-century vantage point; Constantinople was founded in 330 CE, roughly 900 years before Ibn Ezra's time, hence 'less than a thousand years.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:39.962034354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}